## Governance Roles

This model assumes cross-functional participation. A single role may perform multiple functions depending on organizational size, but ownership should remain clear.

| Role | Primary Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Change Requestor | Initiates the change and describes the business need |
| Business Owner | Owns the business outcome and approves readiness for use |
| Technology Owner | Owns technical feasibility, build/configuration, and implementation coordination |
| Product Owner / Process Owner | Clarifies requirements, prioritization, and operational fit |
| Business Analyst | Translates needs into requirements, acceptance criteria, and workflow documentation |
| UAT Coordinator | Organizes testing scope, evidence capture, and defect tracking |
| Tester / Validator | Executes test scenarios and records outcomes |
| Risk / Control Partner | Reviews control implications, evidence sufficiency, and risk treatment |
| Release Manager | Coordinates release timing, dependencies, approvals, and implementation readiness |
| Data Owner / Reporting Owner | Reviews impact on data lineage, reporting logic, or downstream use |
| Approver | Provides required signoff based on role, risk level, or governance policy |
| Post-Implementation Reviewer | Confirms implementation outcome and unresolved follow-up items |

##

## Responsibility Model

A governed change should have explicit ownership across the lifecycle.

| Lifecycle Area | Accountable Role | Supporting Roles |
|---|---|---|
| Business objective | Business Owner | Change Requestor, Product Owner |
| Requirements | Product Owner / Business Analyst | Business Owner, Technology Owner |
| Technical feasibility | Technology Owner | Business Analyst, Release Manager |
| Risk classification | Business Owner / Risk Partner | Technology Owner, Control Partner |
| UAT execution | Business Owner / UAT Coordinator | Testers, Business Analyst |
| Defect disposition | Business Owner / Technology Owner | UAT Coordinator, Risk Partner |
| Release readiness | Release Manager | Business Owner, Technology Owner, Risk Partner |
| Implementation | Technology Owner / Release Manager | Operations, Product Owner |
| Post-implementation review | Business Owner | Technology Owner, Risk Partner, Release Manager |
| Closure | Business Owner / Governance Owner | Supporting stakeholders |

The objective is not to create excessive signoff. The objective is to prevent unclear ownership from becoming hidden implementation risk.

##

## Lifecycle Overview

The model uses the following illustrative lifecycle:

→ Intake Review
→ Draft BRD & FRD
→ Requirements Review
→ Build / Configuration
→ Governance review & approval
→ Development
→ SIT creation, review and approval
→ UAT Ready
→ UAT In Progress
→ UAT Evidence Review
→ UAT completion
→ Production Release Readiness
→ Production deployment & implementation
→ Post-Implementation Review and closure approval
→ Post production issue identification
→ Production Closeout
